The Southbridge SPI register protocol and the NAND/eMMC command sequences in
src/spiex.c and src/xbox.c are ported from:

  * GxOSS/espflasher            (GPL-3.0)
      - balika011    — original PicoFlasher, on which espflasher is based
      - 15432        — eMMC-over-SPI support
      - Hax360       — project overhaul
      - ExposureMG   — ESP32 port

  * balika011/PicoFlasher       — the canonical RP2040 flasher (GPL-2.0)
  * hax360/PicoFlasher (codeberg.org/hax360/PicoFlasher, GPL-2.0)
      - Mate Kukri — discard one SPI read after stopping the SMC (eMMC fix)

The image-build pipeline (src/build_image.c, src/nand_ecc.c, src/xenon_keys.c)
reimplements, for on-device use, the flashing/build workflow that J-Runner
drives through the open-source xeBuild toolchain. The xeBuild *data package*
(patched bootloaders, patch sets, SMC, dashboard files) is NOT included and is
Microsoft-derived; users supply their own copy (the same one J-Runner uses) on
an SD card.

This tool is for working on a console you own. It installs no Microsoft code it
is not given by the user.
